course: dictionary
lesson: 1501
title: Formal words: cease
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cease is a formal word that means to stop happening, or to stop doing something. You will mostly meet it in rules, history books and stories, where writers want to sound careful and serious.
explain: «The voice died away and ceased as an insect's tiny trumpet dwindles swiftly into silence.» The voice got quieter and then stopped, so ceased means stopped. Try swapping in stop: «The voice died away and stopped» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Cease is a verb, so it changes: cease, ceases, ceased, ceasing. It often goes with to, as in cease to exist, which means to stop existing. Once you know the pattern, you can use it too.
fact: Cease means to stop happening, or to stop doing something.
fact: Cease is a formal word, so you will often find it in rules, history and stories.
fact: A ceasefire is a time when fighting stops.
fact: Phrases with cease: cease to exist (stop existing), and never cease to amaze (always amaze).
fact: Cease is a verb: cease, ceases, ceased, ceasing.
exercise: «The rain ceased after an hour.» What does ceased mean? | Began | *Stopped | Grew heavier | Turned to snow
exercise: The tap ceased dripping after ten minutes. Which word means the same as ceased? | Started | *Stopped | Dripped | Filled
exercise: Dinosaurs ceased to exist millions of years ago. What does ceased to exist mean? | *Stopped existing | Were found in a museum | Ran far away | Became bigger
test: «The music ceased, and the room went quiet.» What does ceased mean? | Changed key | Got faster | Started again | *Stopped
test: The old law will cease on 1 May. What does this mean? | It will begin for the first time on 1 May | It will be made stronger on 1 May | It will be written down again on 1 May | *It will stop being in force on 1 May
exam: Which phrase means that something stops existing? | cease fire on the hill | ceasing to care about the rain | *cease to exist | never cease to amaze
